          "content": "```python\nimport re\nfrom collections import Counter\n\n\ndef top_k_words(text: str, k: int) -> list[tuple[str, int]]:\n    \"\"\"Return the k most frequent words in text, sorted by frequency then alphabetically.\"\"\"\n    if k <= 0:\n        return []\n\n    # Lowercase text and extract maximal runs of a-z letters and apostrophes.\n    words = re.findall(r\"[a-z']+\", text.lower())\n\n    # Count word frequencies.\n    counts = Counter(words)\n\n    # Sort by count descending, then word alphabetically, and take the top k.\n    return sorted(counts.items(), key=lambda item: (-item[1], item[0]))[:k]\n```",
